  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 accuracy, a substantial +10.6% improvement over config_001 (same encoder, singleprofile, 0.485), confirming that multiprofile aggregation is a high-impact design choice. However, we have only tested one aggregation method (avgpool) and do not yet know whether a more expressive transformer aggregation can further improve performance. Question: config_003 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding model_setting, profile_setting, and encoder identical to config_002, giving a clean single-variable comparison that isolates the effect of aggregation architecture. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It directly exploits the strongest signal found so far (multiprofile RNA) and tests a logical extension before moving to more complex multimodal settings. (2) The result will tell us whether transformer aggregation is worth the added complexity, which will inform aggregation choices in all future multimodal experiments. (3) It remains in the RNA-only space where signal is strongest, avoiding confounding with the weak image modality (config_010 at 0.208). (4) Under a limited budget, resolving the aggregation question early prevents wasting experiments on suboptimal aggregation in multimodal settings later."
}

